CLAUDE
======

This grammar was written with the help of Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI model
made by Anthropic, used through Claude Code.

Owner and author of the ASH language and of this repository:
  mallionic (The Ashley Project, Mallionic Inc.)

What Claude did:
  - Wrote grammars/ashley.tmLanguage.json (scope source.ashley), based on the
    ASH Pygments lexer from The Ashley Project (docs/ash-guide-src/lexers.py).
  - Covered: keywords (func, class, struct, pub, priv, general, ungeneral,
    static, return, terminate, repeat, loop, ...), types (int8..uint64, ...),
    annotations (@Entry, @naked, @nolibc, @beautycode, @bits, @ovr, ...),
    % directives, strings with escapes and printf placeholders, numbers,
    and asm { } / volatile asm { } blocks with x86 registers.
  - Prepared the GitHub Linguist support for ASH (Ashley): the languages.yml
    entry, heuristics for .ash / .as and samples, on the add-ash-ashley branch
    of https://github.com/mallionic/linguist

All code was reviewed and published by mallionic.

